---
import Site from "../components/Site.astro";
import { link } from "../lib/site";
---

<Site title="Privacy" description="What Market Hub keeps about you and why.">
	<div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-ink">
		<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink-strong">Privacy</h1>
		<p>Market Hub keeps the least it needs to show you your private dashboard and to let you comment. The public pages (markets, quotes, news, opinion) need no account and keep nothing about you.</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">What we keep</h2>
		<ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
			<li>From your Google account, when you sign in: your account id, name, email address and profile picture.</li>
			<li>What you add: the tickers you hold with their number of shares and average cost, and the tickers you follow.</li>
			<li>If you choose to share your portfolio, and only then: the name you pick to be shown under, the tickers you hold with each
				one's share of the portfolio in percent, and the returns of those holdings. Signed-in members see that on the Community
				page. It never includes your name, email or picture, how many shares you hold, what you paid or what it is worth.
				It is off until you turn it on, and turning it off removes it at once.</li>
			<li>The comments you write under opinion articles. They are public, and they are shown with your first name: not with your
				surname, your email address or your picture.</li>
			<li>A session cookie, signed by us, that keeps you signed in for up to 30 days. No advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
			<li>Nothing about you in the analysis tools. Fundamentals Lab and the Earnings Radar, on their own subdomains, read the
				same session cookie only to check that you are signed in; they do not store your name, email or stocks.</li>
		</ul>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">What we do with it</h2>
		<p>
			Show it back to you, and to other members only what you chose to share. To value your positions, the server asks the
			market data provider for the prices of your tickers; it does not send your name, email, share counts or costs.
		</p>
		<p>
			The sentences that read your portfolio back to you are written by a language model run by Anthropic. To write them, the
			server sends it what your portfolio is made of and how it has moved: the tickers, each one's share in percent, and their
			returns. It does not send your name, email or account, how many shares you hold, what you paid or what it is worth, and
			we keep nothing of what the model writes. Nothing is sold, and we do not connect to any broker.
		</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">Where it lives</h2>
		<p>In a Google Cloud Firestore database in the European Union (Belgium region), accessible only to the service.</p>
		<h2 class="pt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink-strong">Your control</h2>
		<p>
			On <a href={link("/account/")} class="link">Account and data</a> you can see and download everything kept about you, and
			delete your account: that removes it from the database at once, takes your portfolio off the Community page and empties every
			comment you wrote. You can also
			delete any comment of yours where it stands.
		</p>
	</div>
</Site>
